CORE
main.i
--arch x86_64 --os linux
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
GCC evaluates function call arguments right-to-left on the x86 family; check
that goto conversion models this: g's side effect (n = n * 2) must take
effect before f's (n = n + 1), giving n == 1. The input is a preprocessed
file so that no target-specific flags are passed to the native preprocessor.
